-- title:
--   Crossing parameter at supersingular j∈{0,1728}: Gauss unit, order one
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and let $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$ be a ring homomorphism to an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ whose zero set is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $a\in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2}=a$, lie in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,k$ (every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no point killed by $q$ other than $0$), and be $0$ or $1728$. Let $K\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, put $A_0=A\cap K$ with reduction $\mathrm{redRestrict}$, and let $\varpi\in A_0$ generate the kernel of that reduction, $e_K\ge 1$ and a unit $\varepsilon$ satisfy $q=\varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$ in $A_0$. Let $R_0$ be the ring of Laurent series $f$ over $K$ for which $f\cdot\Phi(s)=\Phi(r)$ for some $r,s$ in $A_0[X_0,X_1]$ with $s$ not vanishing at $(a,a^q)$ after reduction, where $\Phi$ sends $X_0,X_1$ to the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{jqModC}$, $\mathrm{jqNModC}$ of level $1\cdot q$. Let $G',H',w\in R_0$ with $w$ a unit, $G'H'=\varpi^{\,\mathrm{jWidth}(a)\cdot e_K}w$ (where $\mathrm{jWidth}(a)=3$ for $a=0$, $2$ for $a=1728$, $1$ otherwise), the maximal ideal of $R_0$ equal to $(\varpi,G',H')$, the ideals $(\varpi,G')$ and $(\varpi,H')$ prime with $H'\notin(\varpi,G')$, $G'\notin(\varpi,H')$, and $(\varpi,G')=(\varpi,\Phi(X_1-X_0^q))$, $(\varpi,H')=(\varpi,\Phi(X_0-X_1^q))$. The conclusion is twofold. First, for every $g$ in the base change $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1\cdot q)$ of the full modular function field of level $q$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose underlying Laurent series is $G'$: the series of $\mathrm{frickeInvolutionBar}(1\cdot q)\,g$ lies in the localisation $\mathrm{modularLocalized}(1\cdot q)\,A\,\mathrm{red}$, its image $F$ under $\mathrm{modularRedLocHom}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$ (the subfield of Laurent series over $k$ generated by $\mathrm{jqModC}$ and $\mathrm{jqNModC}$ at level $1$), $F\ne 0$, and the order of $F$ at the place $\mathrm{charLGeomPlaceOfPoint}\,k\,(a^q)$ equals $1$. Second, for all such $g$ and all $g'$ with $g'g=q^{\mathrm{jWidth}(a)}$, the same holds for $g'$ in place of $\mathrm{frickeInvolutionBar}(1\cdot q)\,g$, with order $1$ at the place $\mathrm{charLGeomPlaceOfPoint}\,k\,a$.
--
--   This supplies the two parameter conditions for the wide annulus at a supersingular crossing point of the plane model of $X_0(q)$ in the special cases $j=0$ and $j=1728$, where the local width $\mathrm{jWidth}(a)$ is $3$ or $2$: the Fricke transform of the branch parameter $G'$, and the complementary factor $q^{\mathrm{jWidth}(a)}/G'$, reduce to nonzero functions with a simple zero at the reduced point $a^q$, respectively $a$. It is used in the construction of the two-branch normalisation at such a crossing and in the attachment of the supersingular and opposite annuli in the level-one chart.
